{"mathdb_id": 331888, "uuid": "26947270-2aa6-4f0c-8e9b-9fe62c42367b", "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/331888/bushaw-and-kettle-s-piecewise-turan-number-conjecture-for-di", "title": "Bushaw and Kettle's piecewise Turán-number conjecture for disjoint copies of $P_3$", "statement": "Let $P_3$ be the path on three vertices, let $k$ be a positive integer, and let $ex(n,H)$ denote the maximum number of edges in an $n$-vertex graph containing no subgraph isomorphic to $H$. Write $k\cdot P_3$ for the disjoint union of $k$ copies of $P_3$. **Bushaw and Kettle's conjecture.**

$$
ex(n,k\cdot P_3)=\begin{cases}
\binom{3k-1}{2}+\left\lfloor\frac{n-3k+1}{2}\right\rfloor, & 3k\le n\le 5k-1;\\
\binom{k-1}{2}+(n-k+1)(k-1)+\left\lfloor\frac{n-k+1}{2}\right\rfloor, & n\ge 5k-1.
\end{cases}
$$

